  "worked_solution": "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=2,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF\\,(2)={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{16}{{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{16}{{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16{\\int }_{1}^{2}{t}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16(-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{-2})\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =16(-\\frac{1}{8}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =16(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =16(\\frac{3}{8}) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
